From: GitHub Copilot <copilot@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: robustly install libgsm.a (gsm install flaky on Apple cross)

gsm-1.0-pl22's `gsminstall` target installs libgsm.a, gsm/gsm.h and several
man pages, then marks the library read-only (chmod 444). Under the Mac
Catalyst (macabi) cross toolchain that target hits `make[1]: [gsminstall]
Error 2`, leaving libgsm.a uninstalled, so ffmpeg's unconditional
--enable-libgsm (DEPS_ffmpeg = ... gsm ...) later fails configure with
"ERROR: libgsm not found" and breaks the whole Apple contrib build. On the
iOS / simulator cross the same target succeeds and leaves the 0444 library
in place.

Ignore the gsminstall failure and (re)install the built static library and
public header with `install -m 644`, which unlinks any existing read-only
copy first. This fixes Catalyst (where gsminstall left nothing) without
breaking iOS/simulator (where a plain `cp` would fail "Permission denied"
trying to overwrite the 0444 file); the step is a harmless overwrite where
gsminstall already succeeded.
---
--- a/contrib/src/gsm/rules.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/gsm/rules.mak
@@ -33,4 +33,6 @@ GSM_ENV := GSM_INSTALL_ROOT="$(PREFIX)" \
 .gsm: gsm
 	install -d "$(PREFIX)/lib" "$(PREFIX)/include/gsm" "$(PREFIX)/share/man/man3"
-	$(HOSTVARS_PIC) $(GSM_ENV) $(MAKE) -C $< gsminstall
+	-$(HOSTVARS_PIC) $(GSM_ENV) $(MAKE) -C $< gsminstall
+	install -m 644 "$</lib/libgsm.a" "$(PREFIX)/lib/libgsm.a"
+	install -m 644 "$</inc/gsm.h" "$(PREFIX)/include/gsm/gsm.h"
 	touch $@
